webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9579354Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9679425Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9689397Z ^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9690001Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9691916Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9692609Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9693366Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9694234Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9694764Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9695097Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9695738Z    if you are ready to continue.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9696052Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9696490Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9697067Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9697612Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9697994Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9698178Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9698359Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9698647Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9698854Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9699265Z    can use Nix.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9699407Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9699513Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9699668Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9700011Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9700493Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9703232Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9703397Z I will:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9703860Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9704190Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9704923Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9705623Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9706278Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9706587Z  - install Nix in /nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9706843Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9707218Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9707583Z    /root
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9718438Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9719140Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9729794Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9730353Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9730831Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9732218Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9732820Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9750656Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9751437Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9761602Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9762342Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9762736Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9762927Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9763180Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9763595Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9763827Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9764207Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9764416Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-11T14:32:13.9764505Z If you would like to
